@@ -0,0 +1,23 @@
+---
+id: dl-004-merge-patch-validates-and-returns-independent-json-documents
+type: decision-log
+title: "Merge Patch validates and returns independent JSON documents"
+status: pending
+format: 1
+---
+
+## Context
+
+The toolkit's JSON Patch API validates JSON values and returns a deep-cloned result, ensuring that
+callers' input documents are never mutated. JSON Merge Patch needs matching boundary behavior.
+
+## Decision
+
+Validate and clone both the target and merge patch before applying RFC 7386 processing. Build the
+result from those clones, treating arrays as atomic JSON values and using safe property definition
+for object members.
+
+## Consequences
+
+`applyMergePatch` rejects non-JSON JavaScript values and does not retain references to either input.
+Its merge behavior is predictable alongside `applyPatch` and avoids prototype-key side effects.
